    "created_at": "2026-03-10T08:38:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-10T08:38:18Z",
    "body": "Okay, so that issue suggests scroll restoration happens before `hashchange` and scroll restoration is at least in part an asynchronous process (although vaguely described) as the user agent can do something periodically.\n\nSo to make progress here someone will have to flush out exactly how these all relate. Perhaps they can be synchronous when there is no scroll restoration to be done for instance (assuming we can determine that synchronously).",
